## Object-Oriented cmk
<hr class="section-rule lvl-2">

{{ macros.escape_hatch([
    '[Metaprogramming](@/cmk/metaprogramming), the deep dive on constructors and reflection.',
], mkdocs) }}

CMK's [metaprogramming constructors]({{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming) give it genuine
object-orientation: first-class **classes**, **inheritance** with a linear MRO, and Python-style
**reflection dunders**: all as ordinary cmk-lang, with no new runtime.  Further down, a lighter
alternative fakes the same shapes with zero metaprogramming.

### Classes, Inheritance & Reflection
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

This focused demo shows the object-orientation core: a base class with methods, single-inheritance
override, multiple inheritance with a leftmost-wins MRO, and the reflection dunders each instance
carries.

<div class="def-cards">
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>class NAME[| body |]</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">declare</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body">
      <p>An inline class: methods are recipe targets keyed on <code>${self}</code>, the instance.  Instantiate by callform, or capture with <code>&lt;-</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name">inheritance</span><span class="def-card-kind">linear MRO</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body">
      <p>A class declared with a <code>bases</code> keyword <em>is-a</em> each of those bases: it inherits the whole chain, and overrides a method by redefining it.  When two bases define the same method the <strong>leftmost wins</strong>, as in Python's MRO.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name">reflection dunders</span><span class="def-card-kind">introspection</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body">
      <p>Every instance carries <code>__class__</code>, <code>__doc__</code>, <code>__im_self__</code>, <code>__dir__</code>, <code>__bases__</code>, and more.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>

